-- NVRS wrapper for benchmark/runs/SPE10/SPE10_OPM.DATA.
-- Both Flow and NVRS read that same generated Eclipse deck.
TITLE SPE10 MATCHED TWO-PHASE FIM
FIELDDECK benchmark/runs/SPE10/SPE10_OPM.DATA
PROPSARRAYS 1
-- SPE10 spans nearly eight orders of magnitude in transmissibility.  Flow
-- retains every positive neighbor connection; a global relative cutoff
-- fractures the low-permeability lower channels into artificial islands.
TRANSDROP 0
-- Flow interpolates the deck's SWOF table piecewise linearly; use that same
-- table in the NVRS residual, Jacobian, well controls, and reporting.
FIELDSATFUNC 1
USESCHEDULE 1
REPORTDATES 1

NCOMP 2
MODEL BLACKOIL
OUTDIR benchmark/spe10_matched_nvrs/OUTPUT_SPE10_MATCHED
CASENAME SPE10_MATCHED

-- Fallback constants equal the Eclipse tables. PVTTABLES and ROCK from the
-- FIELDDECK replace them on the device.
PVTCONST 1
PVTTABLES 1
UW 0.3
UO 3.0
BW 1.01
BO 1.01
RS 0
RHOW 1.025181
RHOO 0.848978
CFW 0
CFO 0
CT 4e-6
SWI 0.2
SWR 0.2
PINIT 6000
PBUB 6000
PATM 14.6959
SWINIT 0.2
SGINIT 0
SOINIT 0.8
GRAVITY 1
DARCY 1.127e-3
REFACTOR 0.2
LINSOLVER AMGX

JACOBIAN ANALYTIC
AIM 0
KRYLOV FGMRES
-- CPRW makes the eliminated rate-well/control block visible to the global
-- pressure stage.  At 3e-2 the linear/nonlinear work is balanced: looser
-- solves chop timesteps, while tighter solves overspend in FGMRES.
CPRW 1
LINTOL 3e-2
LINMAXIT 300
-- SPE10's late pressure systems stagnate after repeated short FGMRES cycles.
-- With CGS1, a 60-vector basis cuts full-run linear applications by 55% and
-- wall time by 38%; longer and shorter bases were both slower.
RESTART 60
-- This system retains the same accurate trajectory with CGS1 while avoiding
-- CGS2's second projection, global reduction, and basis update.
ORTHOPASSES 1
AMGFAST 1
AMGREUSE 0
AMGREUSEGROWTH 2.0
MIXED 1
EMULATE 0
STAGE2 JACOBI

-- Flow starts this schedule at one day and carries adaptive dt thereafter.
DTREPORT 1
DTMAX 100
TEND 1000
NEWTONMAX 15
DPMAXREL 0.3
NEWTONSTALLMAX 4
DTKEEP 1
DTCONTROL 1
OPMCONV 1
MBTOL 1e-6
CNVTOL 1e-2
CNVRELAXPV 0.03
CNVRELAXED 1.0
NEWTONTOL 5e-3
LINESEARCH 6
DPMAX 500
DSMAX 0.2
MAXCHOP 12
DTTARGET 10
DTFAILCAP 0.7
-- Once a post-startup step fails, do not relax its learned stability ceiling.
-- This prevents the repeated grow/fail/chop loop seen early in SPE10.  After
-- one cheap (at most two-Newton) accepted solve, cautiously probe a 25%
-- larger ceiling; a failed probe restores the last proven value.  On SPE10
-- this reduces 96 accepted substeps to 66 and improves the pressure and
-- saturation match because the temporal discretisation is closer to Flow.
DTCAPGROW 1.0
DTCAPPROBE 1
DTCAPPROBEITERS 2
DTCAPPROBEFACTOR 1.25
DTMAXGROW 1.5

-- OPM permits completion crossflow. Use the mixture-preserving NVRS branch
-- and the complete injector Schur mode.
WELLXFLOW 2
WELLSCHUR 9
INJBHP 10000

ECLOUT 1
MAKECSV 1
MAKESUMMARY 1
AUTOPLOT 0
WELLPLOT ALL
